## Global

- **One page**, long-scroll. No separate routes.
- **Nav links are in-page anchors** to the section IDs below (sentence case labels).
- **Primary CTA everywhere = book a call** (the Foundation assessment). `[https://calendly.com/ellynsuangani/book-free-ai-consultation?month=2026-08]`
- **Section numbering:** `01 /` … `NN /` in mono, zero-padded, per brand.
- **Layout reference:** structural rhythm modeled on mercury.com — a repeating
  "short declarative banner → cluster of titled blocks" cadence, threaded single CTA, dense footer.
  **Borrow Mercury's structure, not its skin:** Mercury leans on photography, illustrated graphics,
  and autoplay video, all of which the Sonderence design system forbids. Render every beat in
  Sonderence's language — geometric navy/slate node-and-line diagrams, ruled columns, one restrained
  reveal, no photos/video/parallax.
- **Voice rules (from the design system — enforce in all copy):**
  - Headlines: 2–4 words, sentence case, end in a period. No `?`, no `!`, no `:`.
  - Body: one or two sentences, plain, no marketing intensifiers ("seamless", "cutting-edge", "powerful", etc.).
  - UPPERCASE only for labels/eyebrows/tags, always wide-tracked.
  - No emoji. Mixed British/American spelling as in source ("Colour", "-ize" verbs).

